// holdback-op1: operator node 1 of the public demo, and home of the World Durable Object (T-026).
// Test tokens only: SimChain (chain id 31337), or Ethereum Sepolia (11155111) when SETTLEMENT is "sepolia"
// (D41, ADR-0028). Every key the world holds is generated inside the Durable Object, except the Sepolia relayer's,
// the Worker secret SEPOLIA_RELAYER_KEY (apps/demo-cloud/scripts/relayer.mjs); the live-judge keys are secrets too.
// SETTLEMENT picks the world this Worker forwards to, `sim` or `sepolia`; flip it on both files to cut over or back.
// The operator fee (ADR-0023, D33) is read from these variables by the World Durable Object, so it applies to
// both nodes: OPERATOR_FEE_BPS (basis points), OPERATOR_FEE_MIN (base units; 0.01 tUSD is "10000"), and an
// optional OPERATOR_FEE_MAX. Remove both to publish no fee; "0" and "0" publish it at zero. OPERATOR_FEE_GAS (base
// units) is the per-deal gas quote a chain world adds to the minimum (D33 as amended 2026-11-03): 4.70 tUSDC is
// about 1.56 million gas (a deal's three transactions, measured on Sepolia) at its 1 gwei median tip, at the demo's
// fixed, fictional rate of 3,000 tUSDC per test ETH, rounded up. SimChain ignores it.
// For the first wave of pilots all three are "0" (Rafa, 2026-11-12, T-389): a buyer pays the price and the adjudication
// fee only, and Crow's relayer wallet pays the gas. The schedule stays published at 0 so agents read it as before; a
// fee is a parameter (D31), so an operator that anyone else runs can still set one, and these nodes can again.
// Workers Logs keeps console lines (errors, and the World's telemetry lines, T-031) but no invocation logs: those
// record each request's headers, which carry Authorization and the caller's IP (D39).
// Each node answers on its crow.direct and its escrow.stream hostname alike, with no redirect (T-312): agents POST
// signed messages, which many clients will not resend after a redirect, and the EIP-712 domain names no host.
// OPERATOR_URLS is what the nodes advertise: crow.direct.
// T-422 (docs/operator-threat-model.md): FLOOD is this node's flood ceiling, 500 requests per 10 s per client (an IPv4
// address or an IPv6 /64) in each Cloudflare location, answered 429 before the World object; each node has its own
// namespace, so one refusing a client leaves the other's count alone. limits.ts FLOOD_CEILING states the same numbers.
// CF_VERSION_METADATA gives discovery's demo.build.deployedAt (T-413).
// The World object's limits run with this Worker's variables, for both nodes, each node counting apart:
// RATE_READS_PER_MIN and RATE_WRITES_PER_MIN (requests per 60 s), FUNDED_DEALS_PER_CLIENT_PER_DAY (deals the relayer
// funds, about 1.56 million gas each), CIPHERTEXT_BYTES_PER_CLIENT_PER_DAY (new bytes stored; 268435456 is 256 MiB).
// The day is UTC. They protect this operator's service; none caps a value the parties negotiate (D31).
{
  "name": "holdback-op1",
  "main": "dist/worker.js",
  "compatibility_date": "2025-09-15",
  "compatibility_flags": ["nodejs_compat"],
  "workers_dev": true,
  "routes": [
    { "pattern": "api.crow.direct", "custom_domain": true },
    { "pattern": "api.escrow.stream", "custom_domain": true }
  ],
  "preview_urls": false,
  "vars": { "OPERATOR_URLS": "https://api.crow.direct,https://api2.crow.direct", "NODE_INDEX": "0", "SETTLEMENT": "sepolia", "MIN_WINDOW_SEC": "60", "OPERATOR_FEE_BPS": "0", "OPERATOR_FEE_MIN": "0", "OPERATOR_FEE_GAS": "0", "RATE_READS_PER_MIN": "1200", "RATE_WRITES_PER_MIN": "120", "FUNDED_DEALS_PER_CLIENT_PER_DAY": "100", "CIPHERTEXT_BYTES_PER_CLIENT_PER_DAY": "268435456" },
  "ratelimits": [{ "name": "FLOOD", "namespace_id": "4221", "simple": { "limit": 500, "period": 10 } }],
  "version_metadata": { "binding": "CF_VERSION_METADATA" },
  "durable_objects": { "bindings": [{ "name": "WORLD", "class_name": "World" }] },
  "migrations": [{ "tag": "v1", "new_sqlite_classes": ["World"] }],
  "alias": { "node:fs": "./worker/fs-shim.js" },
  "define": { "import.meta.url": "\"file:///holdback/bundle/a/b/worker.js\"" },
  "observability": { "enabled": true, "logs": { "invocation_logs": false } }
}
